1a:["$","div","0",{"className":"analysis-block analysis-paper","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"claim-label claim-paper","children":"Paper Claim"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"将 feedback 信号写成 reflection 文本，存入 memory buffer，在后续行动时作为 context 使用。"}],"$undefined",["$","div",null,{"className":"block-citations","children":[["$","a","paper",{"href":"#reference-paper","aria-label":"来源 1: Reflexion: Language Agents with Verbal Reinforcement Learning · v4","children":["[",1,"]"]}]]}]]}]
1b:["$","div","1",{"className":"analysis-block analysis-inference","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"claim-label claim-inference","children":"Inference"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"沿用论文的编程任务设置作教学演示：输入函数描述，Actor 生成代码与可运行测试；Evaluator 执行可见测试，发现空列表失败。Self-Reflection 将错误概括为“先处理空输入”，写入 Memory。下次 Trial 读取描述和记忆，重新生成程序，最后用未暴露的测试评估。示例输入为构造，原文不同任务的反馈来源各异，不能混用它们的测试权限。"}],"$undefined",["$","div",null,{"className":"block-citations","children":[["$","a","paper",{"href":"#reference-paper","aria-label":"来源 1: Reflexion: Language Agents with Verbal Reinforcement Learning · v4","children":["[",1,"]"]}]]}]]}]
1c:["$","section","mathematics",{"id":"mathematics","children":["$undefined",["$","span",null,{"className":"reading-section-number","children":"06"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Mathematical Foundations"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"section-question","children":"从符号、直觉与简单例子理解理论。"}],[["$","div","0",{"className":"analysis-block analysis-inference","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"claim-label claim-inference","children":"Inference"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"可把 Policy 写成 π(a|state, memory)。Weights 固定，Memory 改变也会改变下一次动作分布，这解释了为什么不做 Gradient Update 仍能适应。Memory Update 将旧记忆与新反思合并，但没有 Bellman 收敛保证；反思文本的质量无法只由长度或语气度量。应将它看作一种有损的经验编码。"}],["$","pre",null,{"className":"math-block","aria-label":"数学表达式","children":"trajectory_t ~ π(· | task, memory_t)\nreflection_t = Reflect(trajectory_t, feedback_t)\nmemory_(t+1) = Update(memory_t, reflection_t)"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"block-citations","children":[["$","a","paper",{"href":"#reference-paper","aria-label":"来源 1: Reflexion: Language Agents with Verbal Reinforcement Learning · v4","children":["[",1,"]"]}]]}]]}]]]}]]}]
1d:["$","section","experiments",{"id":"experiments","children":[[["$","span","results",{"className":"anchor-alias","id":"results"}],["$","span","observation",{"className":"anchor-alias","id":"observation"}]],["$","span",null,{"className":"reading-section-number","children":"07"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Experiments & Claims"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"section-question","children":"Research Question → Experiment → Answer"}],[["$","div","0",{"className":"analysis-block analysis-paper","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"claim-label claim-paper","children":"Paper Claim"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Question：跨 Trial 保存语言反思能否帮助下一次尝试？→ Experiment：在决策、推理和编程任务上比较无反思或不同反馈、记忆设置。→ Answer：作者报告后续尝试的成功率提高；不同环境的评估协议不同，不能把带反馈的重试收益当作完全无反馈的一次作答能力。"}],"$undefined",["$","div",null,{"className":"block-citations","children":[["$","a","paper",{"href":"#reference-paper","aria-label":"来源 1: Reflexion: Language Agents with Verbal Reinforcement Learning · v4","children":["[",1,"]"]}]]}]]}],["$","div","1",{"className":"analysis-block analysis-paper","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"claim-label claim-paper","children":"Paper Claim"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"作者在顺序决策、编程与语言 reasoning 任务中报告相对 baseline 的改善。"}],"$undefined",["$","div",null,{"className":"block-citations","children":[["$","a","paper",{"href":"#reference-paper","aria-label":"来源 1: Reflexion: Language Agents with Verbal Reinforcement Learning · v4","children":["[",1,"]"]}]]}]]}]]]}]]}]
1e:["$","section","takeaways",{"id":"takeaways","children":["$undefined",["$","span",null,{"className":"reading-section-number","children":"08"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Takeaways"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"section-question","children":"这篇论文改变了哪些判断？"}],[["$","div","0",{"className":"analysis-block analysis-inference","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"claim-label claim-inference","children":"Inference"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Reflexion 中的学习状态主要是 Episodic Memory。评估时至少记录 Trial Index、可见 Feedback 与 Memory Reset 规则，否则同名的 pass@1 很容易被误读成同样预算的一次尝试。"}],"$undefined",["$","div",null,{"className":"block-citations","children":[["$","a","paper",{"href":"#reference-paper","aria-label":"来源 1: Reflexion: Language Agents with Verbal Reinforcement Learning · v4","children":["[",1,"]"]}]]}]]}]]]}]]}]
1f:["$","section","assumptions",{"id":"assumptions","children":[[["$","span","limits",{"className":"anchor-alias","id":"limits"}]],["$","span",null,{"className":"reading-section-number","children":"09"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Most Fragile Assumption"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"section-question","children":"哪一个假设失效会动摇方法？"}],[["$","div","0",{"className":"analysis-block analysis-inference","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"claim-label claim-inference","children":"Inference"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"最脆弱的假设是失败原因可从现有轨迹辨认。随机失败、隐藏环境状态和不完整测试可能诱导错误归因；一旦写入 Memory，错误建议会影响更多尝试。"}],"$undefined",["$","div",null,{"className":"block-citations","children":[["$","a","paper",{"href":"#reference-paper","aria-label":"来源 1: Reflexion: Language Agents with Verbal Reinforcement Learning · v4","children":["[",1,"]"]}]]}]]}],["$","div","1",{"className":"analysis-block analysis-inference","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"claim-label claim-inference","children":"Inference"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"这里的学习通过 reflection memory 实现，并不更新 model weights；效果也依赖 feedback 是否可靠。"}],"$undefined",["$","div",null,{"className":"block-citations","children":[["$","a","paper",{"href":"#reference-paper","aria-label":"来源 1: Reflexion: Language Agents with Verbal Reinforcement Learning · v4","children":["[",1,"]"]}]]}]]}]]]}]]}]
20:["$","section","reproduction",{"id":"reproduction","children":["$undefined",["$","span",null,{"className":"reading-section-number","children":"10"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"One-Week Reproduction"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"section-question","children":"用一周检验一个最小且明确的命题。"}],[["$","div","0",{"className":"analysis-block analysis-hypothesis","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"claim-label claim-hypothesis","children":"Hypothesis"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Day 1–2：准备带明确错误类型的小编程任务。Day 3–5：比较无 Memory、原始错误日志、压缩反思三组，限制相同重试次数。Day 6–7：替换任务中的表面变量，测教训能否迁移，并报告错误反思造成的额外失败。"}],"$undefined",null]}]]]}]]}]
21:["$","section","counterexample",{"id":"counterexample","children":["$undefined",["$","span",null,{"className":"reading-section-number","children":"11"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Counterexample Design"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"section-question","children":"如何构造有辨识力的反例？"}],[["$","div","0",{"className":"analysis-block analysis-hypothesis","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"claim-label claim-hypothesis","children":"Hypothesis"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"让某些失败来自随机超时，另一些来自真实逻辑错误，并隐藏该区分。若 Agent 从一次超时推断出错误算法规则，再在正常环境中持续避开正确动作，就能验证语言记忆可能放大偶然事件。"}],"$undefined",null]}]]]}]]}]
22:["$","section","follow-up",{"id":"follow-up","children":[[["$","span","outlook",{"className":"anchor-alias","id":"outlook"}]],["$","span",null,{"className":"reading-section-number","children":"12"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Follow-up Research"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"section-question","children":"从缺陷与需求推导新的研究问题。"}],[["$","div","0",{"className":"analysis-block analysis-prior","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"claim-label claim-prior","children":"Prior Work"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"后续相关工作 DoCtOR 已将失败归因、反事实步骤修正与定向 Reflection 结合，用于 Multi-Agent Collaboration。单独提出因果归因或定向反思已有接近的研究。"}],"$undefined",["$","div",null,{"className":"block-citations","children":[["$","a","2608.28264v1",{"href":"#reference-2608.28264v1","aria-label":"来源 3: Finding Where the Buck Stops: An Automated Failure Attribution-Based Reflection Framework for Multi-Agent Collaboration","children":["[",3,"]"]}]]}]]}],["$","div","1",{"className":"analysis-block analysis-hypothesis","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"claim-label claim-hypothesis","children":"Hypothesis"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"让每条反思携带一个可执行的反事实检查：若原因真是空输入，那么非空输入应通过，空输入应失败。系统通过主动实验决定是否保留记忆。相对 ReAct 的即时观察利用，这研究的是可证伪的经验积累；需要检验它是否减少错误归因，而不只是增加调试次数。 提案应进一步面对多个错误相互抵消或共同致错的情况：在写入跨任务规则前，主动选择能区分竞争原因的干预，并检验规则在未见任务上的可识别性。若只定位单个决定性错误，研究就没有覆盖这个新增问题；是否足够新颖仍需更多相关工作检索。"}],"$undefined",["$","div",null,{"className":"block-citations","children":[["$","a","2210.03629",{"href":"#reference-2210.03629","aria-label":"来源 2: ReAct: Synergizing Reasoning and Acting in Language Models","children":["[",2,"]"]}],["$","a","2608.28264v1",{"href":"#reference-2608.28264v1","aria-label":"来源 3: Finding Where the Buck Stops: An Automated Failure Attribution-Based Reflection Framework for Multi-Agent Collaboration","children":["[",3,"]"]}]]}]]}]]]}]]}]
